# Commands hachiko never reports about, one glob per line, matched against the
# command's name and against its full path. Everything here is expected to be
# running on this Mac — spending a core for an hour at a time, or sitting there
# with nothing waiting on it — so an alert about it would be noise and the next
# real one would be read as more of it.
#
# Both of the watches over processes read this file: the one that reports half a
# core held for an hour, and the one that reports a process a finished session
# left sitting in a checkout.
#
# A pattern is a glob, not a regular expression, and it has to match the whole
# name or the whole path.

# The docker VM. Its helper runs the Linux guest, so a busy container is this
# process at 100% for as long as the build takes.
OrbStack
OrbStack Helper
*/OrbStack.app/*

# A UTM guest, and the hypervisor underneath it. A Windows VM idles at a few per
# cent and pegs a core whenever Windows feels like it.
UTM
QEMULauncher
qemu-system-*

# Spotlight. Indexing is off on this Mac, so these should never be busy at all —
# listed because a macOS update turns indexing back on and the first thing it does
# is walk every worktree's node_modules for an hour.
mds
mds_stores
mdworker
mdworker_shared
mdbulkimport

# Time Machine, which checksums the whole of a backup set and has no idea anybody
# is waiting.
backupd
backupd-helper

# A macOS update, which downloads and verifies in the background by design.
softwareupdated
SoftwareUpdateNotificationManager

# The window server and the kernel's own accounting process. Neither is something
# a session can do anything about, and WindowServer is busy whenever Screen
# Sharing is connected.
WindowServer
kernel_task
